<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			22/5/97		  15/5/97	     24/5/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	    600		  575-600		   400</p>
<p>    Naphtha	     100		   75-100		 50-75</p>
<p>    Gas oil   1,600-1,650		    1,650		 1,475</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	    425		  400-425		   350</p>
<p>    Jet kero	     15		    10-15		    25</p>
<p>Gasoline stock movements were again brisk with a little material going trans-Atlantic as well as some into Germany.</p>
<p>Naphtha stocks rose simply because of product arrivals.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks dipped as no material arrived, but some left for markets down the Rhine and in Benelux.</p>
<p>Fuel oil stocks rose slightly with arrivals of straight-run. Some vacuum gas oil departed for Germany and some cracked product left for the bunker sector.</p>
<p>Jet fuel inventories were slightly higher.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom, +31 20 504 5004</p>
